WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:54.170
<b>The City of Water, Water Seven</b>

3
00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:55.570
[NAMI]
In order for
Luffy and Robin

4
00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.270
to get some rest and recover,

5
00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.740
the Going Merry
remained anchored off

6
00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:01.340
the uninhabited
island for four days.

7
00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.510
After that, we set sail.

8
00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.850
Today marks the third morning since we
resumed our voyage.

9
00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.650
The weather is clear and sunny.

10
00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:11.310
Mostly spring, with occasional bouts of
summer.

11
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.490
It's beautiful!

12
00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:22.550
[SANJI]
Nami! Looook!

13
00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:26.990
I made this potato paille

14
00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.270
especially for you,
mademoiselle.

15
00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:30.530
I hope you enjoy it.

16
00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.100
Delicious!

17
00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.860
[SANJI]
That makes me so happy!

18
00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:37.900
Hey! Keep it down, jerk!

19
00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:40.070
Some people are trying to sleep around
here!

20
00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:41.910
Sorry about that, cactus head.

21
00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.610
My most sincere apologies.

22
00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.460
What, you cigarette
snorkeling dartboard?!

23
00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:48.030
[SANJI]
Huh?
What did you call me?

24
00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.870
[SANJI]
Dartboard. Dartboard eyebrows.

25
00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:51.870
[SANJI]
What?!

26
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:57.620
[USOPP]
Lu...

27
00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.090
[CHOPPER]
...ffy!

28
00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:57.090
[CHOPPER]
...ffy!

29
00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:58.120
[CHOPPER]
...ffy!

30
00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.330
[USOPP]
Lu...

31
00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.460
Hey!

32
00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.500
[BOTH]
– Whoo!
– Whoo!

33
00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:05.890
We've been waiting for this!

34
00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.460
Luffy!

35
00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:16.270
This is me, frozen!

36
00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:23.480
[laughter]

37
00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:26.350
Ugh, I can't believe
this is how he behaves

38
00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:28.480
after almost freezing to death.

39
00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:30.650
Whataya think?

40
00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:31.580
[USOPP]
You nailed it!

41
00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:34.080
That's exactly what you looked like!

42
00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.380
[NAMI]
Make sure you
clean all that up, Luffy!

43
00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:38.350
'Kay! Hey Nami, is that food?

44
00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:39.510
What are you eating?

45
00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:41.290
Some potato paille.

46
00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:44.080
Potatoes, huh? I love potatoes!

47
00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.740
Sanji! Make me some!

48
00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.510
Just how many hours
a day to you have

49
00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.110
to lie around and sleep, anyway?

50
00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:50.250
That's none of your business!

51
00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.650
I'll sleep as long as I like.
Wanna fight about it?

52
00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:54.740
[SANJI]
You're still
recuperating,

53
00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:55.740
but that hasn't slowed

54
00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:58.040
your appetite down in
the slightest, has it?

55
00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.620
So this is paille, huh?
Good stuff!

56
00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:08.090
Why is it called that?

57
00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.820
Because the meat is taken

58
00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:12.530
from the tail of the
giant beast Paille.

59
00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.430
I should know.
I was the one who killed it.

60
00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.630
It was over 100 meters long!

61
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.460
Whoa! 100 meters?!
That's amazing, Usopp!

62
00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.610
And I did it all before breakfast.

63
00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:24.260
[CHOPPER]
Wait, you
woke up early to kill it?

64
00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:27.470
Chopper, have you forgotten who I am?

65
00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:31.510
[CHOPPER]
Oh! I get it!
You're Captain Us...

66
00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:34.610
Yes! That's right! I am the
great and almighty Captain Uso...

67
00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.240
[NAMI]
Robin!

68
00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:42.510
[SANJI]
Robin! Good to see you!

69
00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.580
[CHOPPER]
Robin!

70
00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:46.510
Are you feeling okay?
Do you still have a chill?

71
00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.150
Your treatment helped me out tremendously.

72
00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.480
Thanks! You're a
wonderful doctor!

73
00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:55.150
Calling me a wonderful doctor
won't make me happy

74
00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:57.390
or anything, you stupid jerk.

75
00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.180
[USOPP]
He sure looks happy.

76
00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:58.880
[LUFFY]
Yep.

77
00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:00.330
You should take it easy, Robin.

78
00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:01.470
Luffy's already recovered enough

79
00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:05.170
to where he's running around
and screaming like an imbecile.

80
00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.300
But you can just relax and take your time.

81
00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.120
[LUFFY]
Yeah!

82
00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:09.480
That wasn't a complement!

83
00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:10.690
Hey, Robin!

84
00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.380
Would you like me to make you something to
warm you up?

85
00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.310
Do you have an appetite?

86
00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:16.610
I do.

87
00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.310
May I have some coffee, please?

88
00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:20.680
[SANJI]
Of course! It's my pleasure!

89
00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:36.850
Hmm?

90
00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.650
What the heck is that?

91
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.570
Man, this paille
stuff is delicious!

92
00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:50.540
I can't stop eating it!

93
00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:52.210
Yeah, I know!

94
00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.430
I bet we could make some
money selling this stuff.

95
00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:55.800
Luffy, come quick!

96
00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.540
There's a... There's a
frog doing the front crawl!

97
00:05:58.570 --> 00:05:59.540
[LUFFY]
What?

98
00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:01.830
See for yourself!
It's headed to your side!

99
00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:02.890
Really?

100
00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:04.740
I wonder if it's that same frog we heard
about.

101
00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:05.540
Come on, Luffy.

102
00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:06.500
Are you really
gonna take anything

103
00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:09.390
that goofy Admiral
told you seriously?

104
00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.690
There's no way a frog
would do the front crawl.

105
00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:12.570
It's... HOLY CRAP!

106
00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.730
THERE'S A FROG DOING
THE FRONT CRAWL!

107
00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:16.370
[LUFFY]
Come on! After him!

108
00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:17.370
[ZORO, USOPP, and CHOPPER]
– Aye, aye!
– Aye, aye!

109
00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.480
[LUFFY]
Take in the sail!
Stand by the oars!

110
00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:21.380
Bring the ship
about to 2 o'clock!

111
00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.100
[ZORO, USOPP, and CHOPPER]
– Aye, aye!
– Aye, aye!

112
00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.050
[LUFFY]
Hurry!

113
00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:24.070
[ZORO]
I don't know why,

114
00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:26.970
but I get the feeling we
really have to follow it!

115
00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.280
Sorry to keep you waiting, mademoiselles.

116
00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.350
Uhh... what's happening?

117
00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.550
What the...? What's going on?

118
00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:39.960
It seems like the ship has changed its
course.

119
00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:42.040
Hey! What's the deal here?

120
00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.620
Why'd you change our course without asking
me?

121
00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:46.420
Nami! You're never
gonna believe it!

122
00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:48.870
We found this huge frog
with scars all over its body

123
00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:50.310
and we're following it!

124
00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.820
A frog? What?

125
00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:52.750
We have to catch up to it,

126
00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:55.490
capture it, cook it,
and eat it for lunch!

127
00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:57.220
You wanna eat it?!

128
00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:00.520
[NAMI]
You're right!

129
00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.120
Huh...

130
00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.230
Is that a lighthouse?

131
00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:06.450
Now what's a lighthouse
doing way out here?

132
00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.500
I wonder if anyone lives there.

133
00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:10.670
[LUFFY]
What's up?
Do you see an island?

134
00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:12.640
Not really.
It's just a lighthouse.

135
00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:15.270
There's not enough there
for the Log Pose to point to.

136
00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.370
What about the frog?

137
00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.100
Tell us which way the frog went!

138
00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.240
Not a chance!

139
00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.540
It looks like the frog is headed to the
lighthouse.

140
00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:24.080
Frogs should be
marinated in white wine

141
00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.190
to dissolve the mucus.

142
00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:27.780
Then, you coat them with
flour and fry them up crisp.

143
00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:29.180
Sanji! Snap out of it!

144
00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:31.840
If the Captain says
we're going after the frog,

145
00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.880
we really don't have
much choice in the matter.

146
00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:35.820
Robin...

147
00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.390
[LUFFY]
Let's go! Full speed ahead!

148
00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:39.390
[ZORO, USOPP, and CHOPPER]
– Aye, aye!
– Aye, aye!

149
00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:41.790
[NAMI]
Why are you all
going along with this?!

150
00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:45.200
[ZORO, USOPP, LUFFY and CHOPPER]
– Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!
– Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

151
00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:51.620
[LUFFY]
It's flying!

152
00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.450
Quick! Don't let it get away!

153
00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.450
Let's get up ahead of it
and block its course!

154
00:07:55.490 --> 00:08:00.520
[ZORO, USOPP, LUFFY and CHOPPER]
– Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!
– Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

155
00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.880
I guess we ran
ashore or something!

156
00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:19.390
Nami, Robin! Say something!
Are you two okay?

157
00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.980
Yeah, I think I'm okay.

158
00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.580
Same.

159
00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.880
[relieved]
Oh...
Thank goodness.

160
00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:27.730
[bell clanging]

161
00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:28.730
Huh?

162
00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.730
What is that sound?

163
00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.860
What the heck? What's going on?

164
00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:43.110
[distance distant whistle]

165
00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:50.420
Wait, that sounds like a...

166
00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:01.330
No way! Out here?!

167
00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:07.120
[NAMI]
Full reverse! Right now!

168
00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:09.730
Turn 180 degrees!

169
00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.840
[LUFFY]
Whoa! That was close!

170
00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:35.210
[USOPP]
That hunk of
metal's trying to kill us!

171
00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:36.340
[CHOPPER]
Is it a ship?

172
00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:38.240
No way! Something
that big and heavy

173
00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:40.210
shouldn't even
be able to float!

174
00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:46.250
Hey, what're you doing?!
Get out of the way!

175
00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.890
[growls]

176
00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:57.130
Oh no! Froggy!

177
00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.560
It looked like it was spitting out smoke!

178
00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:35.610
[CHIMNEY]
Pirates?

179
00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.270
Granny! Granny!
Look! We got pirates!

180
00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:40.440
[KOKORO]
What?
Izzat true, Chimney?!

181
00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.390
Okey dokey then, in that case.

182
00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:46.300
Better bring Granny
the Transponder Snail!

183
00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.050
It's gonna be big pain
if they call for help

184
00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:50.450
and the marines show up.

185
00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:51.710
What should we do?

186
00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.690
[CHIMNEY]
Here it is, Granny!

187
00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:56.550
[KOKORO]
Uhm... hello?

188
00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:59.090
Who is this?

189
00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.560
Sorry, you got the wrong number.

190
00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:03.220
She's totally drunk!

191
00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.760
[KOKORO]
Oh! Paille, huh?

192
00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:13.540
That stuff goes good with booze!

193
00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.640
[CHIMNEY]
Mm-mm! Yummy!

194
00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.280
<b>Chimney
Kokoro's Grandchild</b>

195
00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:17.060
My name's Chimney.

196
00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.670
This is our kitty cat, Gonbe

197
00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.240
<b>Gonbe
A Cat (Actually a Rabbit)</b>

198
00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:20.690
and that's Granny Kokoro.

199
00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:23.530
<b>Stationmaster Kokoro
Shift Station</b>

200
00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.140
You fellas wouldn't happen

201
00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:25.100
to be train robbers, would ya?
Wahahaha!

202
00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:27.980
My name's Luffy and I'm
gonna be King of the Pirates.

203
00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:28.550
Really?

204
00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:29.380
Yep.

205
00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:32.190
Hahahaha!
I like you, you're funny!

206
00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:35.200
By the way, Chimney. That
thing's a steam boat, right?

207
00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.740
Seems awfully long to me.

208
00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:38.670
Can't imagine it getting very far.

209
00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:39.670
[CHIMNEY chuckles]

210
00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:41.510
You've probably never
seen anything like this.

211
00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:44.140
Seeing as it's the
only one in the world.

212
00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.010
It's not a steam boat,

213
00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:48.130
it's a sea train
called the Puffing Tom.

214
00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:48.860
[NAMI]
How does it work?

215
00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:50.300
It uses a steam engine to turn

216
00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:52.800
its paddlewheels
and run on a railway.

217
00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:56.700
Railway?

218
00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:57.700
[CHIMNEY]
Uh-huh! If you look close,

219
00:11:57.740 --> 00:12:00.340
you can see the tracks
right below the waves.

220
00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:02.310
The train goes the
same route every day,

221
00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:04.580
taking people from
one island to the next.

222
00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:07.440
It carries ships and packages and other
stuff, too.

223
00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:09.850
Oh wow, funny we
didn't notice it before.

224
00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:11.320
Didn't you see the signal?

225
00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:13.180
There's a bell
ringing and everything!

226
00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:14.650
How were we supposed to know?!

227
00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:15.950
And if we couldn't figure it out

228
00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:18.520
then that frog sure
wouldn't get it, would he?

229
00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.520
It was awful rude of you to hit him like
that.

230
00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:22.390
We were gonna catch him and cook him,
you know.

231
00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:25.410
Oh, you saw the frog?
That's Yokozuna.

232
00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:27.080
[LUFFY]
He sure was an awesome swimmer.

233
00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:28.880
[CHIMNEY]
Either way,
I wouldn't worry about him,

234
00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:30.310
he's pretty tough.

235
00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:31.710
In fact, that
wasn't the first time

236
00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.650
he's challenged
the train and lost.

237
00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:35.020
He's really kind of a pain.

238
00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:36.080
If you want to see him again,

239
00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:38.050
just hang around here
and I'm sure he'll pop up.

240
00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.590
That's why he didn't run.

241
00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:41.160
Wow, I thought
that frog was stupid,

242
00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.830
but it turns out he was
just being super manly.

243
00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:44.830
[CHIMNEY]
Easy for you to say!

244
00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:46.990
You don't have to put up
with him all the time!

245
00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.130
I can't even count
how many times

246
00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:49.960
he's broken the rail guard.

247
00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.010
And just imagine what it's like

248
00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:54.110
for the passengers when
he slams into the train!

249
00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:55.700
That's pretty crazy.

250
00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.900
Okay, since that
frog's a fighter like me,

251
00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.660
I'm not gonna eat him after all!

252
00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:01.980
Who would want to eat that gross thing in
the first place?

253
00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:05.980
Anyways, after this, where're
you folks headed off to?

254
00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:09.080
The sea train runs to all sorts of places.

255
00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:14.010
There's the town of the
Spring Queen, St. Poplar.

256
00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:18.880
There's the gourmet town, Pucci
or the Carnival town, San Faldo.

257
00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:20.880
They're all fun places to go.

258
00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:22.620
And if you happen to
work for the government,

259
00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:23.780
you can take a special train

260
00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.230
that's even fancier than the Puffing Tom.

261
00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:27.700
Good, then that's the
place we're gonna g...

262
00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:28.840
Give it up!

263
00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:31.140
Thanks, but there's no reason
for us to take the train

264
00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:32.500
when we have our own ship.

265
00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:33.700
We'll just follow the log.

266
00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:35.750
Oh? Where's it pointing to?

267
00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:37.660
Should be someplace east of here.

268
00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:41.530
I see. Well, in that case
it's Water Seven for sure.

269
00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.100
The train you saw
on the way here

270
00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:46.140
just came from
Blue Station on that island.

271
00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:48.140
They call it the City of Water.

272
00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:50.860
They got great shipyards.

273
00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:52.930
You might say that's their claim to fame.

274
00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:55.570
When it comes to boats,
they're first class!

275
00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:56.840
They're always
coming up with some

276
00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:59.800
fancy new technology to build
boats for the World Government.

277
00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.090
Whoa, then they must have
some awesome shipwrights, too!

278
00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:06.440
[KOKORO]
Some? More like
damn near all of 'em!

279
00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:08.910
City's like a regular
shipwright's convention!

280
00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:10.410
Ah! You hear that?!

281
00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:11.800
Yeah!

282
00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:13.350
All right then. It's settled!

283
00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:15.320
We're gonna find the best
shipwright in Water Seven

284
00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:16.720
and get him to join our crew!

285
00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:20.890
Oh, is that so?
In that case, hold on a sec.

286
00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.320
Upsey-daisy, you can do it.

287
00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:24.300
Where's she going?

288
00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:25.800
Dunno.

289
00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.090
I got a present for ya.

290
00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:30.680
This is a little map of the city and a
reference letter.

291
00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:32.810
Just give this to a
fella named Iceburg,

292
00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:35.550
and I promise he'll
fix yer ship up good.

293
00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.700
Water Seven's a
pretty confusing place,

294
00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:39.800
be sure not to get lost.

295
00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.600
You have a big
heart, don't you?!

296
00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:43.340
We really owe you one!

297
00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.210
[CHIMNEY]
We'll be heading
back to Water Seven soon,

298
00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.780
so maybe we'll see you there.

299
00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:52.520
[KOKORO]
Sounds like a plan to me!

300
00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.250
And if you like,
I can even give you folks

301
00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:56.390
a tour of all my
favorite drinkin' holes!

302
00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:57.780
Ha ha ha!

303
00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:00.490
Sounds good! We'll try
to keep a look out for you!

304
00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:01.890
It'll take 'bout a
week for the Log

305
00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.460
to lock onto the next island,

306
00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:06.560
so you'll have plenty of
time to do some sightseeing!

307
00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:08.900
[LUFFY]
Great! Should be fun!

308
00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:13.270
[LUFFY]
Okay! Everyone
ready?! Time to set sail!

309
00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:14.750
[CREW]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

310
00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:16.680
Thanks again for the map and reference
letter.

311
00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:19.490
I sure am glad we
ran into you on the way!

312
00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:26.540
[CHIMNEY]
Have a safe trip!

313
00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:29.440
Better keep an eye out

314
00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:32.360
for all those government
types down there!

315
00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:34.930
[LUFFY]
Yahoo! Let's go!

316
00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:37.770
City of Meat, here we come!

317
00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:39.500
[USOPP]
Did you forget
where we're going already?

318
00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:51.690
[NAMI]
What a nice wind!

319
00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:52.980
We might make it
out to Water Seven

320
00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.850
even faster than I thought!

321
00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:56.150
I'll be happy either way!

322
00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:57.750
[SANJI]
Don't worry
about finding a shipwright.

323
00:15:57.970 --> 00:15:59.440
I got it all under control.

324
00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.470
I'll get the hottest girl
in town, guaranteed.

325
00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.140
What do I care if
the shipwright's hot?!

326
00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:06.180
I want a huge, manly dude... like
even bigger than a bear!

327
00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:07.450
16 feet tall!

328
00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:09.480
A guy that size couldn't
even fit on the ship!

329
00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:11.620
And who knows how much
food he would need to eat!

330
00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:14.270
All that matters is that he's good at his
job.

331
00:16:14.270 --> 00:16:15.940
If you ask me, the
real problem's gonna be

332
00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:17.070
finding someone crazy enough

333
00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:19.080
to go sailing with
a bunch of pirates.

334
00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:20.060
Size doesn't matter!

335
00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:22.120
I'm just glad we're
gonna make a new friend!

336
00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:24.420
We're lucky we ran into that train station
on the way.

337
00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:26.470
This map should be a big help!

338
00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.440
All we have to do is
follow Kokoro's directions

339
00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:31.500
to that Iceburg guy
and we're set!

340
00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:32.380
<b>Around here</b>
<b>Water 7</b>

341
00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:33.210
I see.

342
00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:34.550
Stupid drunk!

343
00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.510
Whoa, looks like Luffy's art.

344
00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:39.720
<b>Shipwright</b>
<b>meters</b>

345
00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.340
Okay, let's try to
find a shipwright

346
00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:39.950
that looks
something like this!

347
00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.090
If I saw a guy like that, I'd run.

348
00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:43.140
I wouldn't just run,

349
00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:45.780
I'd jump into the sea to get away from
that freak.

350
00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.220
But he looks like he
might be part-octopus,

351
00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:49.320
so even that
might not save me.

352
00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:51.390
Don't you have anything better to talk
about?

353
00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:53.330
[NAMI]
Okay everybody, since
we're gonna be at Water Seven

354
00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:55.720
for a whole week, let me
give you your allowance.

355
00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:59.200
[CHOPPER]
Ooh! Me first!
Me first! Ah! Stop shoving!

356
00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:02.200
[sounds of arguing]

357
00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:06.350
[LUFFY and USOPP]
– Allowance! Allowance! Allowance!
– Allowance! Allowance! Allowance!

358
00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.000
[LUFFY]
Why're you hugging
the ship, Usopp?

359
00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:20.400
I know all these tin plates
might not look like much to you,

360
00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:23.340
but they bring back a lot
of fond memories for me.

361
00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:25.810
I almost hate to see them go,
but it'll all be worth it

362
00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:28.080
if the Merry can finally
get the repairs she needs!

363
00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:29.880
[SANJI]
I feel the same way.

364
00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:31.850
I'm proud of her battle
scars like anyone else,

365
00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:32.980
but she's taken a real beating

366
00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:35.150
since we've entered
the Grand Line.

367
00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:38.320
The deck squeaks and we've got leaks
popping up everywhere.

368
00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:39.460
Nobody wants to admit it,

369
00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:42.070
but if we don't fix this soon,
we're as good as sunk.

370
00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:43.570
[LUFFY]
Yeah, but even if
we can't get a shipwright

371
00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:45.940
for the crew, we still
have plenty of money!

372
00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:47.210
We can do more
than just fix her;

373
00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:48.880
we can power her up, too!

374
00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:50.880
[USOPP]
Ooh!
Then let's get more cannons!

375
00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.860
[LUFFY]
Yeah! And a big statue!

376
00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:54.990
[ZORO]
Hey, I think we're there.

377
00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:55.990
Huh?

378
00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:01.500
[LUFFY]
He's right!
I can see Water Seven!

379
00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:05.100
[LUFFY]
All right men, time to row!

380
00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:06.090
[SANJI]
The wind's enough.

381
00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:08.760
Don't wear us out before we even get
there.

382
00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:20.070
Lovely.

383
00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:23.280
Wow.

384
00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:29.080
<b>Water Seven
"The City of Water"
Grand Line</b>

385
00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:31.350
[LUFFY]
Nobody told me
it was gonna be this cool!

386
00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:37.120
[LUFFY]
Whoa!
Check that thing out!

387
00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.930
I didn't know they made fountains that
big!

388
00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:42.930
OHHH!

389
00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:45.870
That's nuts! I've never
seen anything like it!

390
00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:47.540
And I thought the
sea train was a big deal.

391
00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:50.340
At any rate, that's the station up front.

392
00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:54.010
[NAMI]
Must be the same one
Kokoro was talking about.

393
00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:55.810
Still, I wonder
where the harbor's at?

394
00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:57.810
Inside the town, maybe?

395
00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.510
[FISHERMAN A]
Hey! Hold on!

396
00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:02.070
Pirates shouldn't
sail in the front,

397
00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:03.100
you gotta be more discreet!

398
00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:07.040
Use the backstreet entrance
over there, instead!

399
00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.200
[NAMI]
Oh, okay! Thank you!

400
00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:18.070
Whoa. Look,
there's so many boats!

401
00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:22.310
Awesome! The city's floating!
I wonder how it works?!

402
00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.320
[CHOPPER]
But everything's
flooded everywhere!

403
00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:35.190
Aren't all the buildings gonna be full of
water, too?

404
00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:37.290
Not at all. The houses
here were built

405
00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:39.120
with a submerged
foundation in mind.

406
00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:40.220
[CHOPPER]
Hmm?

407
00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:43.180
If you look beneath the walkway,
you'll understand.

408
00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:44.060
[CHOPPER]
You're right!

409
00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.990
It's like the city's
sitting on stilts!

410
00:19:46.020 --> 00:19:48.260
I see. Certainly
lives up to its name.

411
00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:51.120
Hey, hurry up! Dock the ship!

412
00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:55.940
Whoa, hold on a sec!

413
00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:58.370
What do you pirates think
you're doing here in town?!

414
00:19:58.370 --> 00:20:00.580
You're not looking to
plunder, now are you?

415
00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:03.280
Nuh-uh! We just wanna
get our ship repaired!

416
00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:05.530
[USOPP]
He just asks that
like it's no big deal?

417
00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:08.400
In that case there's a
little cape just ahead of here.

418
00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:10.520
Anchor your ship
over there for now!

419
00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:12.270
[NAMI]
Okay!

420
00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:13.910
[LUFFY]
Thanks for the help!

421
00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:15.080
[USOPP]
They keep waving us off.

422
00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:18.310
[ZORO]
Of course they do.
We're flying a pirate flag.

423
00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:21.900
[USOPP]
Should be okay
to anchor here, right?

424
00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:23.130
[SANJI]
Can't see why not.

425
00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:25.070
It's certainly far enough from the city.

426
00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:27.770
[LUFFY]
Works for me! Furl the sail!

427
00:20:33.470 --> 00:20:35.350
[CREW cries out in surprise]

428
00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:37.080
Are you trying to
break the ship?!

429
00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:40.750
No! All I did was pull
the rope like I always do!

430
00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:45.990
Holy crap! If the Merry's
falling apart this easy

431
00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:48.160
we're lucky we
made it here at all!

432
00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:51.200
By the way, they're not scared of pirates
here, are they?

433
00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:52.830
Don't you think
that's kinda strange?

434
00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:55.870
It's cause we're shipyard
customers just like anyone else.

435
00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.540
Stop yapping and start fixing the ship
already!

436
00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:00.170
They probably aren't
concerned about pirates

437
00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:02.540
because they have enough
security to deal with them

438
00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:03.460
if they misbehave.

439
00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.190
Bet there's plenty
of Marines here, too.

440
00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:06.930
Comes with the territory, huh?

441
00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:08.500
What, are you kidding me?!

442
00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:09.980
You mean they're gonna
have us arrested?!

443
00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:11.110
I don't think
that'll be a problem,

444
00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:13.050
since we're paying
customers and all.

445
00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:14.260
[USOPP]
I guess so.

446
00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:16.190
[LUFFY and USOPP]
– Well, that settles it! We'll see you later!
– Well, that settles it! We'll see you later!

447
00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:18.030
Hold on one minute, you two!

448
00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:20.500
[NAMI]
I need you to come with me

449
00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:22.700
to take care of some business.

450
00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:25.440
What business?

451
00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:27.740
First off, we're going to
take Kokoro's reference letter

452
00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:30.170
to this Iceburg guy... assuming
we can find him.

453
00:21:30.210 --> 00:21:31.610
Hopefully, he'll be
able to take care of

454
00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:33.130
the Merry's repairs for us.

455
00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:34.980
After that, we'll
have to find a place

456
00:21:35.010 --> 00:21:37.140
where we can trade in
our gold for some berries.

457
00:21:37.180 --> 00:21:38.750
[LUFFY]
Okeydokey. Works for me!

458
00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:40.520
So what are we waiting for?

459
00:21:40.550 --> 00:21:42.920
Let's go! To Water Seven!

460
00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:45.520
[NAMI]
Okay, but aren't
you forgetting the gold?

461
00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:50.220
[MAN F]
Hey! Some pirates
are causing a ruckus at Dock #1!

462
00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:52.250
[MAN G]
What?! That's not good!

463
00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.620
[MAN H]
Come on!
We'd better go check this out!

464
00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:59.500
<b>A Shipyard
Water Seven</b>

465
00:21:55.690 --> 00:21:58.190
[PAULIE]
Sorry, but you're
not making any sense.

466
00:21:58.230 --> 00:21:59.900
[MIKAZUKI]
Need me
to talk slow for you?

467
00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:03.510
<b>Dock One</b>

468
00:21:59.930 --> 00:22:03.800
Hahahaha!

469
00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:09.090
<b>Captain Mikazuki
Big Helmet Pirates
Bounty: ¬36 Million</b>

470
00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:06.340
Soooooo you
repaired our ship.

471
00:22:06.370 --> 00:22:09.300
Sooooo then I got to thinking.

472
00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:11.070
And no matter
how I looked at it,

473
00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:13.720
no matter how many times
I turned our little deal

474
00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:15.760
around in my head,
I still felt like you

475
00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:18.120
were charging me way too much.

476
00:22:18.160 --> 00:22:20.330
You're interrupting our job.

477
00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:21.430
[MIKAZUKI]
Here's the deal.

478
00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:24.970
I'm not paying a single
berry for the work you did.

479
00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:27.100
[MIKAZUKI CREW laughs]

480
00:22:27.140 --> 00:22:30.770
[MIKAZUKI CREW A]
Thanks for
the repairs, they were great!

481
00:22:30.810 --> 00:22:34.180
[MIKAZUKI CREW B]
So kind
of you to do them for free!

482
00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:46.420
[ICEBURG]
Mmwell... Kalifa.

483
00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:47.790
You know what's going on?

484
00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:49.020
[KALIFA]
Yes, Mr. Iceburg.

485
00:22:49.060 --> 00:22:51.060
Those pirates are
Dock One customers.

486
00:22:51.090 --> 00:22:54.760
But now that the work's done, they refuse
to pay.

487
00:22:54.800 --> 00:22:56.900
Sexual harassment.

488
00:22:56.930 --> 00:23:00.070
Mmwell. Maybe it is.

489
00:23:07.020 --> 00:23:10.050
[MIKAZUKI CREW laughs]

490
00:23:10.080 --> 00:23:12.560
Listen, Sir, we take
our jobs very seriously.

491
00:23:12.590 --> 00:23:14.960
It's not wise to mock our shipwrights like
that.

492
00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:27.940
[MIKAZUKI CREW A]
Captain!

493
00:23:30.040 --> 00:23:32.010
[CARPENTER A]
Oops. Sorry!

494
00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:32.770
Hey jerk!

495
00:23:32.770 --> 00:23:34.610
Watch where you swing that thing!

496
00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:37.810
You just knocked out our... Ahh!

497
00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:40.720
[KAKU]
Oops. Sorry.

498
00:23:40.750 --> 00:23:43.480
Hey, you punks
trying to pick a fight?!

499
00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:45.350
Who do you think you are?!

500
00:23:55.130 --> 00:23:56.300
Oh yeah.

501
00:23:56.300 --> 00:23:56.820
We haven't had a chance to
test fire that cannon, have we?

502
00:23:56.820 --> 00:23:57.520
Aww! It looks like I missed
my chance to go with them.

503
00:23:58.430 --> 00:23:58.940
Really?! Can we
go to a bookstore?

504
00:23:58.940 --> 00:24:00.940
No. Not yet.

505
00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:05.480
Damn you!

506
00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:07.910
You won't get away with this!

507
00:24:07.940 --> 00:24:10.350
We'll be back! Just wait!

508
00:24:23.350 --> 00:24:28.860
<b>Galley-La Company
A Shipbuilding Firm, Water Seven
(Purveyors to the World Government)</b>

509
00:24:23.630 --> 00:24:25.300
You're on shipwright turf.

510
00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:26.460
This is what
happens when you try

511
00:24:30.660 --> 00:24:33.060
[USOPP]
Maybe we should trade in
the gold before anything else.

512
00:24:33.090 --> 00:24:35.430
That's boring. I wanna
go to the shipyard.

513
00:24:35.460 --> 00:24:36.530
It might not matter to you,

514
00:24:36.560 --> 00:24:38.660
but I'd feel nervous
walking around a crowded city,

515
00:24:38.700 --> 00:24:41.000
dragging a giant bag of treasure behind
me.

516
00:24:41.030 --> 00:24:43.570
If we trade it, we'll still
be dragging berries around.

517
00:24:43.600 --> 00:24:45.040
I know, but it'll
be a lot smaller,

518
00:24:45.070 --> 00:24:46.670
so people won't
notice it as much.

519
00:24:46.830 --> 00:24:48.730
I mean, what if we
run into thieves?!

520
00:24:48.730 --> 00:24:50.380
[LUFFY]
Ha! We are thieves!

521
00:24:50.760 --> 00:24:53.030
Well, that's true
but if we cash it in,

522
00:24:53.070 --> 00:24:55.100
you won't be the only
one carrying the money.

523
00:24:55.130 --> 00:24:57.640
I don't know if I like the sound of that.

524
00:24:57.640 --> 00:25:00.110
It's almost like you don't
want me taking care of the gold!

525
00:25:00.150 --> 00:25:02.850
Yep! Only you could
lose that much gold!

526
00:25:02.880 --> 00:25:04.950
He already forgot it once today.

527
00:25:04.980 --> 00:25:07.750
[LUFFY]
You guys don't
trust me, your own captain?!

528
00:25:07.750 --> 00:25:08.840
[NAMI and USOPP]
– Nope!
– Nope!

529
00:25:08.840 --> 00:25:10.880
[LUFFY]
Awww... Hey, that
really hurts my feelings!

530
00:25:10.910 --> 00:25:12.840
I don't know if
I can keep sailing

531
00:25:12.880 --> 00:25:15.280
with a crew that...
Wait, what's that?

532
00:25:15.310 --> 00:25:16.710
[NAMI]
Huh. That's funny.

533
00:25:16.740 --> 00:25:19.540
Is that the only entrance to the city?

534
00:25:19.580 --> 00:25:21.310
What's a rental bull shop?

535
00:25:21.310 --> 00:25:22.210
[LUFFY]
Beats me.

536
00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:24.450
Obviously they must
rent out something.

537
00:25:24.480 --> 00:25:25.750
Yeah, but what's a bull?

538
00:25:25.780 --> 00:25:28.720
I dunno like a bulldog?

539
00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:30.000
That can't be right.

540
00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.520
[LUFFY]
Excuse me!
We'd like to rent some bulls!

541
00:25:32.590 --> 00:25:35.460
Find out what they are first!

542
00:25:35.490 --> 00:25:37.630
[SHOP MAN A]
Hi, looking
for some bulls, you said?

543
00:25:37.660 --> 00:25:38.560
How many people?

544
00:25:38.600 --> 00:25:39.460
We've got three.

545
00:25:39.500 --> 00:25:40.560
[SHOP MAN A]
What kind would you like?

546
00:25:40.680 --> 00:25:44.010
There's three ranks.
"Yagara," "Rabuka," and "King."

547
00:25:44.070 --> 00:25:44.970
For your little group,

548
00:25:45.010 --> 00:25:47.510
I'm thinking two
Yagaras will do just fine.

549
00:25:47.540 --> 00:25:49.380
Gimme one rare
and one well-done.

550
00:25:49.410 --> 00:25:51.380
You don't know what
you're saying, do you?!

551
00:25:51.700 --> 00:25:54.440
[SHOP MAN A]
Oh? You
followed a Log to get here?

552
00:25:54.440 --> 00:25:55.160
[LUFFY]
Yep!

553
00:25:55.390 --> 00:25:56.220
[SHOP MAN A]
That's quite an achievement,

554
00:25:56.260 --> 00:25:57.420
but if you're not
from around here,

555
00:25:57.460 --> 00:25:59.930
this is probably the first
time you've heard about bulls.

556
00:26:00.170 --> 00:26:01.370
Uh-huh.

557
00:26:01.400 --> 00:26:03.430
[SHOP MAN A]
Well, to make a
long story short there they are!

558
00:26:03.430 --> 00:26:05.930
Yagara bulls, you can
find them all over town.

559
00:26:06.160 --> 00:26:08.720
As you can see, it's a
type of fish that swims

560
00:26:08.760 --> 00:26:10.160
with its head above the water.

561
00:26:10.190 --> 00:26:11.790
Since the whole city is flooded,

562
00:26:11.830 --> 00:26:14.160
we have a lot more
canals than walkways.

563
00:26:14.200 --> 00:26:16.000
Because of that,
pretty much everyone

564
00:26:16.030 --> 00:26:18.270
here uses the bulls
in their daily life.

565
00:26:18.280 --> 00:26:21.050
If you want to go sightseeing,
you'll need one too.

566
00:26:21.080 --> 00:26:23.060
So they use the bulls to pull those little
boats?

567
00:26:23.060 --> 00:26:25.520
Actually, the boat part's
mounted on their back.

568
00:26:25.560 --> 00:26:27.360
In other words,
it's not much different

569
00:26:27.420 --> 00:26:29.480
than riding
horseback on land.

570
00:26:31.790 --> 00:26:33.790
Go ahead and take a look
at the bullpen over there

571
00:26:33.820 --> 00:26:36.860
if you want to pick one out.
They don't bite.

572
00:26:36.890 --> 00:26:40.860
It'll be 2,000 berries for
two two-passenger Yagaras.

573
00:26:40.880 --> 00:26:41.980
[NAMI]
They're cute!

574
00:26:42.010 --> 00:26:46.080
They even look like horses!

575
00:26:46.120 --> 00:26:49.780
Ugh! That's gross! What's
wrong with you, horse fish?!

576
00:26:49.840 --> 00:26:53.470
Ha! Since that one seems to like
you, I'll mount him for you.

577
00:26:59.180 --> 00:27:01.390
Is he all right
carrying heavy stuff?

578
00:27:01.530 --> 00:27:03.240
Yeah, these guys are built for power.

579
00:27:03.270 --> 00:27:05.800
The people here use them for moving all
the time.

580
00:27:05.840 --> 00:27:08.640
That's a big bag.
Can I ask what's inside?

581
00:27:08.680 --> 00:27:09.580
[LUFFY]
Gold.

582
00:27:10.770 --> 00:27:13.580
That's a good one. Well,
whatever it is, it'll be okay.

583
00:27:13.580 --> 00:27:14.080
See?

584
00:27:14.080 --> 00:27:15.120
Whoa! Gimme!

585
00:27:15.280 --> 00:27:16.310
Yeah, right!

586
00:27:16.370 --> 00:27:18.370
I guess he thought it was worth asking,
at least.

587
00:27:18.380 --> 00:27:20.680
This is why I said I don't trust you with
the money!

588
00:27:20.720 --> 00:27:23.090
I had to show him...
He didn't believe me!

589
00:27:23.130 --> 00:27:25.200
Wow, I sure wasn't expecting that.

590
00:27:25.240 --> 00:27:26.400
Like I said,

591
00:27:26.440 --> 00:27:28.940
that'll be one million berries
for the two Yagara bulls.

592
00:27:28.970 --> 00:27:30.940
Don't try to change the price on us!

593
00:27:31.340 --> 00:27:33.480
Speaking of gold, do you know where we can
get ours cashed in?

594
00:27:33.510 --> 00:27:35.580
Well there's quite a few places,

595
00:27:35.620 --> 00:27:37.950
but you'd probably
clean them all out trying

596
00:27:37.980 --> 00:27:40.120
to trade in that much
treasure in one shot.

597
00:27:40.150 --> 00:27:41.220
If I were you,

598
00:27:41.250 --> 00:27:43.260
I'd check out downtown
on the shipbuilding island.

599
00:27:43.400 --> 00:27:45.180
We're not really familiar with the area.

600
00:27:45.180 --> 00:27:47.080
Think you could give us some directions?

601
00:27:47.110 --> 00:27:48.910
It's right over there.

602
00:27:48.950 --> 00:27:49.950
Here, take this.

603
00:27:49.980 --> 00:27:52.180
Oh! A map!

604
00:27:52.500 --> 00:27:53.670
Thanks for the help!

605
00:27:53.750 --> 00:27:56.560
[LUFFY]
Hey, we can find a
shipyard downtown too, right?

606
00:27:56.590 --> 00:27:58.960
Yep! Best one in the world!

607
00:27:59.010 --> 00:28:00.210
That'll be perfect.

608
00:28:00.250 --> 00:28:01.180
We can head straight

609
00:28:01.220 --> 00:28:03.190
to the shipyard soon
as we trade in our gold!

610
00:28:03.230 --> 00:28:05.030
Well you're not gonna
hear any complaints from me.

611
00:28:05.060 --> 00:28:07.170
As long as the Merry
gets repaired, I'll be happy!

612
00:28:07.200 --> 00:28:08.530
Then we'll find a shipwright.

613
00:28:08.570 --> 00:28:10.900
Oh man, I can't wait!

614
00:28:10.900 --> 00:28:11.580
Well?

615
00:28:11.580 --> 00:28:12.550
Shall we?

616
00:28:12.550 --> 00:28:15.890
Yeah! Go Yagara!

617
00:28:15.920 --> 00:28:16.890
[SHOP MAN A]
See you later!

618
00:28:17.300 --> 00:28:20.630
Thanks for your business and have a safe
trip!

619
00:28:21.330 --> 00:28:26.270
[LUFFY]
Downtown,
full speed ahead! Yahoo!
